{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "🤖 Tour 6: AI & Gemini Integration Pipeline",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/api_internal/routes/ai.ts",
      "line": 20,
      "description": "### 🤖 The Gemini Core Integration: `callGemini`\n\nThis unified function handles all Generative AI API operations. We make HTTP POST requests directly to Google's Gemini endpoint utilizing the lightning-fast **`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview`** model. We configure `thinkingLevel: \"minimal\"` (Line 29) to achieve optimal response latency and reduce processing costs!"
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/api_internal/routes/ai.ts",
      "line": 90,
      "description": "### 💭 Dynamic Study Prompts: Ponder Questions\n\nThe `/generate-ponder-questions` endpoint crafts a tailored facilitator prompt based on the user's active chapter (Line 103-110). It strictly enforces a response in the user's target language, focusing on \"Personal Application\" to make daily study approachable."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/api_internal/routes/ai.ts",
      "line": 134,
      "description": "### ⚡ Dual-Layer Performance Caching\n\nTo avoid redundant translation requests and save costs, we generate an **MD5 hash signature** of the text, language, and type (Line 134). Before calling Gemini, we query a centralized `translation_cache` collection. If a match is found, we serve it instantly!"
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/api_internal/routes/ai.ts",
      "line": 251,
      "description": "### 📦 Batch Translations mapping (JSON Prompts)\n\nTo translate the dashboard's active chat list efficiently, the `/translate-batch` route bundles multiple messages in a single query (Line 303-312). We prompt Gemini to return a clean JSON map (`{\"msg_id\": \"text\", ...}`), which we parse dynamically and write back to Firestore in one atomic batch."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/api_internal/routes/ai.ts",
      "line": 406,
      "description": "### 📝 Personal Weekly Recaps & Cooldowns\n\nThe `/generate-personal-weekly-recap` endpoint summarizes a user's study notes from the past 7 days into an encouraging personal letter. To prevent abuse, we enforce a strict **6-day generation cooldown** (Line 430-448), serving cached letters if requested too early."
    }
  ]
}
